<<<
sentence, in grammar, means a set
===
**sentence,** in grammar, means a set
>>>

<<<
If it contains one or more CLAUSES, it is a complez s. ; if its subject consists of more than one parallel noun &c., or its predicate of more than one verb &c., it is a compound s. ; if its subject or predicate or verb (or more) is understood, it is an elliptical sentence.
===
If it contains one or more ^^CLAUSES^^, it is a *complex s.*; if its subject consists of more than one parallel noun &c., or its predicate of more than one verb &c., it is a *compound s.*; if its subject or predicate or verb (or more) is understood, it is an *elliptical sentence.*
>>>

